<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Rwanda</h1><p class="st-meta">1962 CE – present · capital Kigali</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small, densely populated republic of the Great Lakes, which suffered the 1994 genocide against the Tutsi and has since been rebuilt under the RPF.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rwandan-revolution">Hutu revolution</a> of 1959 to 1961 abolished the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-rwanda">Kingdom of Rwanda</a>, the country became independent from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ruanda-urundi">Belgian Ruanda-Urundi</a> on 1 July 1962 as a republic led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregoire-kayibanda">Gregoire Kayibanda</a> and his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parmehutu">Parmehutu</a> party. Hundreds of thousands of Tutsi fled abroad as violence against them recurred.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregoire-kayibanda">Kayibanda</a>'s <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-first-republic">First Republic</a> was overthrown in 1973 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juvenal-habyarimana">Juvenal Habyarimana</a>, who ruled a one-party state. In 1990 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rwandan-patriotic-front">Rwandan Patriotic Front</a>, formed by Tutsi exiles in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/uganda">Uganda</a>, invaded. After Habyarimana's plane was shot down in April 1994, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> extremists organised a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> that killed some 800,000 people, mostly Tutsi, in about 100 days, until the RPF took power in July.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rwandan-patriotic-front">RPF</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-kagame">Paul Kagame</a>, president since 2000, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-rwanda">Rwanda</a> has rebuilt its economy and institutions, held community gacaca courts and switched to English as a main language, while critics point to restrictions on political freedom. It remains a republic with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kigali">Kigali</a> as capital.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/rwanda.jpg" alt="Rwanda" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown Vector: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Rwanda.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1962 CE – present</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kigali</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gregoire Kayibanda, Juvenal Habyarimana, Paul Kagame</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kinyarwanda, French, English, Swahili</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Rwanda</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Rwanda</dd></dl></aside></div>
